lines=['# Lantern head-edge audit','', 'Read-only production audit. Coordinates and row/frame indices are zero-based. Atlas coordinate = (132*frame+x,164*row+y). Source SHA256 f7cd414a9a12596d28c4b6c101453a1a87ff7c3a37deec54d40f50d0f3c16ecc; 1188x2952 RGBA; 132x164 cells.','', '## Findings','', 'Pale/gray crown and temple boundary pixels are present, especially idle c2/c3 and lobby c0/c6. All listed pixels are fully opaque, so these are baked RGB fringe, not partially transparent white matte. Walk c2 has cyan on the scalp boundary. Bright whites inside eyes and chest emblems are intentional and must be preserved.','', 'The table lists selected boundary pixels for focused review, not an automatic deletion mask. Conservative correction: replace neutral fringe on the connected head contour with the existing dark outline sampled from the adjacent outline on the same frame; preserve occupied silhouette. Remove only demonstrably exterior protrusions after inspecting the crop. Cyan on the bald scalp is a stronger removal/correction candidate; do not globally remove green, white, or gray. Dark gray boundary colors below 100 remain review-only in boundary-candidates.json.','', '|row|frame|local x,y|atlas x,y|original RGBA|recommendation|','|---|---|---|---|---|---|']
